    "title": "Supervised hashing on CIFAR-10 — does a better projection pay?",
    "note": "Class-mAP on CIFAR-10 (512-d ResNet-18 features, class-based relevance, mean ± std over 3 splits) at a matched 8-byte budget, against full-precision float (2 KB) and product quantisation (64 B). At a fixed quantiser the story is the projection axis: a random code (LSH) trails the float, a learned unsupervised rotation (ITQ) edges past it, supervision (GRH, KSH) more than doubles it at 256x less memory, and a deep hash head (DPSH) — the pairwise objective trained on the same frozen features and labels — is higher still. Evidence for the lens, not a submittable board; reproduce with the paper's benchmark harness (train_deep_hash.py + run_cifar_supervised.py --deep).",
